<Legal
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Porphyra's marketing site sets no tracking cookies. Here's exactly what we do use."
  lastUpdated="2026-08-07"
>
  <p>
    Short version: our marketing site (the pages you're reading right now) sets no cookies
    and needs no consent banner, because there's nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>Marketing site (porphyra.example)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Umami analytics</td><td>Cookieless</td><td>Aggregate page views and referrers — no persistent identifier, self-hosted, never shared with a third party.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>The app (app.porphyra.example)</h2>
  <p>
    Once you have an account, the app sets one strictly-necessary session cookie to keep you
    logged in. It's not used for tracking or advertising, and it's not shared with any third
    party. Under GDPR/ePrivacy, strictly-necessary cookies don't require consent — but we're
    telling you it exists anyway.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Stripe (billing) and our AI provider may set their own cookies or use their own
    tracking when you interact with their embedded flows directly — see their respective
    privacy policies. Full list in our <a href="/legal/subprocessors">subprocessors page</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
